# Spec-first workflow

Three governing docs, in order of authority:

1. `PRD.md` — approved requirements/architecture (what & why, see §14 sign-off).
2. `TDD.md` — implementation detail, currently complete only for M0–M2. M3+ is
   deliberately stubbed (§9) — do not design those domains ahead of the
   milestone that actually picks them up.
3. `EPICS.md` — one Epic per PRD milestone, Stories sized as tracker issues,
   each citing the PRD §/TDD § it implements.

Rules:

- New work should map to an existing Story in `EPICS.md`. If it doesn't,
  amend the docs first — usually a small addition — rather than building
  untracked scope.
- Don't implement a later story's deliverable as a side effect of an earlier
  one; check the story's own plan for an explicit scope boundary before
  reaching for "while I'm here" changes.
- Monorepo layout: root `pubspec.yaml` is the Dart pub workspace (Melos 7
  config lives under its `melos:` key — there is no separate `melos.yaml`).
  `packages/dart_sysinfo` is Flutter-free (no `flutter:` SDK constraint,
  ever). `packages/dart_sysinfo_flutter` may depend on `dart_sysinfo`; never
  the reverse. `packages/native` is a Rust crate and is **not** a Dart
  workspace member.
